Description: Count each drawing of an icon the theme has in stereo
 While KIconEngine draws, the loader also says whether the icon it gives has a stereo picture
 (in either eye of a window drawn once per eye, or as the plain icon outside an eye pass); the
 engine then adds one to the application's _q_stereo_icons_drawn. Whatever draws windows once per
 eye (the KDE platform theme, an item in Qt Quick) learns from it which windows show such icons.
 The check is remembered under the plain icon's cache key, and is skipped with no lookup when no
 theme in the tree has stereo folders, so a theme without them behaves as before.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-22
